WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:06.320
The ‘90s were full of bucket hats, boy bands,&nbsp;
and television stars. But many of the TV icons&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:11.200
of the era have disappeared in the years since.&nbsp;
You've probably thought about your '90s favorites&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:15.040
from time to time, so we've checked in&nbsp;
on a few to see what they're up to now.

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:21.600
Arguably the coolest teen on ‘90s TV, Marla&nbsp;
Sokoloff rose to fame as Stephanie Tanner's best&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:27.280
friend Gia on Full House. She wore crop tops,&nbsp;
went to make-out parties, and even smoked--in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:33.200
short, her character had attitude to spare. Marla&nbsp;
went on to star in Whatever It Takes where she met&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:39.200
James Franco, who she ended up dating for four&nbsp;
years. Her sitcom and film career was on fire.

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:44.240
So where did Marla Sokoloff go? The short&nbsp;
answer is that she's been as busy as ever,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:49.440
even if it's been in projects that may not put her&nbsp;
in the limelight. Marla has had consistent work,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:54.160
including six seasons as Lucy Hatcher on&nbsp;
The Practice, an assortment of television&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.160 --> 00:01:00.800
guest-starring roles, and a slew of made-for-TV&nbsp;
movies. Between 2016 and 2020, Sokoloff has also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:06.560
reprised her role as Gia on the Full House sequel&nbsp;
series Fuller House, making our '90s hearts swell.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:12.960
At the age of 11, Tatyana Ali lit up the small&nbsp;
screen as Ashley Banks on The Fresh Prince of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:17.840
Bel-Air. We watched her have her first kiss,&nbsp;
belt out a song for a record label, and grow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:23.440
out her bangs. After Fresh Prince, Ali expanded&nbsp;
her talents to the music industry and film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:28.480
putting out the album Kiss the Sky in&nbsp;
1998 and appearing in the film Jawbreaker&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:34.400
with Rose McGowan and Judy Greer. In the years&nbsp;
following, Ali made education her top priority,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:39.680
and she graduated from Harvard with a Bachelor's&nbsp;
Degree in African-American studies and Government.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:45.440
Tatyana later married Stanford professor Dr.&nbsp;
Vaughn Rasberry and is a proud mother of two.

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:49.440
Still, she hasn't completely abandoned&nbsp;
the industry; in recent years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:53.600
she's branched out into producing, and&nbsp;
her later acting credits include the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:59.120
2018 holiday film Jingle Belle. Plus, get&nbsp;
ready to break out your best Carlton dance:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:04.480
Tatyana and her castmates got together for&nbsp;
a Fresh Prince reunion special on HBO Max.

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:09.040
Before Hermione Granger, there was&nbsp;
another big-haired overachiever&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:11.520
named Topanga Lawrence on Boy Meets World.

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:13.760
“Topanga”

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:17.480
“Topanga!”

00:02:17.480 --> 00:02:21.200
“Topanga!”

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:26.800
Danielle Fishel was the envy of every '90s kid&nbsp;
until the sitcom ended in 2000. While Fishel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:32.320
had small roles on Yes, Dear and Longshot after&nbsp;
the series ended, she ultimately found that good&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:37.680
roles just weren't coming her way. She took some&nbsp;
time off from acting to earn a psychology degree,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:42.320
worked at Bloomingdales, got married,&nbsp;
divorced, and even received a DUI.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:48.400
In 2008, she began to host The Dish, which&nbsp;
showcased her bubbly personality. More recently,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:53.440
Danielle reunited with her old castmates on the&nbsp;
Boy Meets World sequel series Girl Meets World,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:57.600
remarried, had a baby, and has her&nbsp;
eyes set on the director's chair.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.600 --> 00:03:02.320
Sadly, she didn't end up with Ben Savage in&nbsp;
real life, but it's nice to see her happy.

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:09.040
Before Wikipedia, pre-teens had one go-to&nbsp;
source of information: Clarissa. Melissa Joan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:14.080
Hart explained it all and we loved every second of&nbsp;
it. Just when it didn't seem like she could be any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:19.440
cooler, Hart took on the lead role in Sabrina the&nbsp;
Teenage Witch. Living with her two awesome aunts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:24.880
and the best talking cat on TV, Sabrina used&nbsp;
her magical powers to get through high school.

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:29.840
Even though those characters were magical, Hart&nbsp;
says she was only seen as her iconic roles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:35.040
and getting parts after Sabrina was a struggle.&nbsp;
During this frustrating time, she met her husband,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:39.440
Course of Nature lead singer Mark Wilkerson.&nbsp;
The couple have been going strong ever since,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:45.040
and have three boys together. In 2010, Hart's&nbsp;
acting career took off again with a co-lead&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:50.480
role in Melissa and Joey alongside fellow '90s&nbsp;
heartthrob Joey Lawrence. Hart has also been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:55.920
busy in the holiday movie game as the lead in The&nbsp;
Santa Con, Broadcasting Christmas, A Very Merry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.920 --> 00:04:01.600
Toy Store, A Very Nutty Christmas, Christmas&nbsp;
Reservation, and Dear Christmas. So for now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:05.760
you can get your holiday cheer on with Melissa&nbsp;
Joan Hart while you hold your breath for that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:10.240
rumored Clarissa Explains It All reboot.&nbsp;
And speaking of classic Nickelodeon...

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:15.120
“Welcome to GoodBurger home of the&nbsp;
GoodBurger can I take your order?”

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:19.920
In the ‘90s, you couldn't imagine a&nbsp;
better sketch duo than Kenan and Kel.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:23.920
We all know Kenan Thompson went on&nbsp;
to make us laugh every week on SNL,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:27.920
but if you're wondering what happened to&nbsp;
the other half of the duo, you're not alone.

00:04:27.920 --> 00:04:32.880
Kel Mitchell has actually had a fascinating&nbsp;
career since his time on Good Burger. He's now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:39.360
a voice actor, with his most famous role being&nbsp;
"T-Bone" on Clifford the Big Red Dog. In 2019,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:44.480
Mitchell also appeared on Dancing with the Stars,&nbsp;
and ended in second place. Another surprising&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:49.360
career turn came later in the year, when he&nbsp;
announced he'd become a licensed youth pastor.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:54.640
The father of three rediscovered his faith after&nbsp;
a struggle with drugs and alcohol. He told People,

00:04:54.640 --> 00:04:58.240
"I was trying to figure it all out on&nbsp;
my own. But what I needed to do was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.240 --> 00:05:02.720
turn to Him. Once I found that clarity with&nbsp;
Christ, I knew everything would work out."

00:05:04.146 --> 00:05:08.560
Lark Voorhies came into our lives as the&nbsp;
extraordinary Lisa Turtle on Saved by the Bell.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:12.640
Afterwards, Voorhies made appearances on&nbsp;
shows like The Bold and the Beautiful,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:18.160
In the House, and The Parkers. Unfortunately, she&nbsp;
also became part of a National Enquirer scandal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:22.640
when the publication claimed that Voorhies&nbsp;
was hospitalized due to a cocaine addiction.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.640 --> 00:05:26.720
Lark filed a lawsuit suggesting that she&nbsp;
lost work because of their false claims.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:29.840
She remained out of the limelight&nbsp;
even after the case concluded.

00:05:30.880 --> 00:05:34.320
“And now, for all the dirt the&nbsp;
National Enquirer hasn’t found out yet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:37.840
here’s Lisa our galloping gossip.”

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:43.040
Voorhies publicly said she'd like to&nbsp;
be involved with the Saved By The Bell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.040 --> 00:05:46.880
reboot — and those pleas have paid&nbsp;
off, as she popped up on an episode&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.880 --> 00:05:51.840
of the show. We wish her the same amount of&nbsp;
happiness she brought all of us in the '90s.

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:57.040
Shane West burst into the TV scene on&nbsp;
the ABC family drama Once and Again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.040 --> 00:06:01.200
later leaving the small screen to take&nbsp;
roles in the films Whatever It Takes and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:05.360
Get Over It and falling in love with&nbsp;
Mandy Moore in A Walk to Remember.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:09.920
He became an undeniable heartthrob —&nbsp;
and then he was gone -- but not really.

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:14.880
West actually went back to his roots, working&nbsp;
regularly on television, although the roles were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:18.800
a little different than his fans were&nbsp;
used to. After years of teen romance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:24.080
West decided to leave that world behind and&nbsp;
take on grittier parts, including roles on ER,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.080 --> 00:06:29.760
Salem, Gotham, and Nikita. West has also continued&nbsp;
to work regularly on the film side of things,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:34.080
with a list of credits that includes&nbsp;
the thriller Escape the Field.

